-- ============================================================================
-- Generated by scripts/generate-roll-forming-machines-migration.js; re-run it and diff instead of editing.
--
-- Sheet Metal Roll Forming is costed (user decision 2026-11-22). Migration 862 seeded its 125 line machines for the USA only, at the
-- memory files' "World Average" rates (memory/Sheet metal roll forming/Machines), not a country's; no machine for India; and no material group for the process.
--
-- 1. USA: direct and indirect overhead (USD/hr, to cents) from memory/Countries data/Netherlands_XML_Data_.csv (the user's decision: no export lists the
--    USA, as for Hydroforming, migration 1109), and the USA labour of the process's wage grade (memory/Sheet metal roll forming/roll_forming_wage_grades.csv;
--    the rate most of that grade's HR Rates rows carry): 4 - Metal 43.21, 3 - Metal 36.30, 0 - Metal (the coil as supplied) 0.
--    A row is changed only while it still holds the World Average rates 862 seeded, so a rate entered in HR Rates is kept.
--    e.g. the default mill Bradbury 2.5" Shaft Diameter 12 stand: 22.22 + 15.25, labour 43.99 -> 25.06 + 14.95, labour 43.21.
-- 2. India: the twins of all 125 (memory/Countries data/India_XML_Data_.csv, commodity "Sheet Metal - Roll Forming"): each machine's own overheads and the India
--    labour of the grade, 4 - Metal 2.30, 3 - Metal 1.73, 0 - Metal 0; specs as the USA twin's (e.g. the default mill
--    17.97 + 1.26, labour 2.30).
--    The 14 exports list the same 125 machines and agree on each machine's own data (setup time, line speed, strokes per minute,
--    coil load time, stands, shaft, stock limits), which is the World Average files' (checked when this file is generated).
-- 3. process_material_groups: Sheet Metal Roll Forming draws on its own material group (its 102 materials, memory/Sheet metal roll forming/Raw Materials/material_master.csv, migration 855).
